; asymmetric binary operations: sub, div, power, mod, max, min, atan2.
; unlike monoid ops, these are NOT commutative: f(a,b) ≠ f(b,a).
; they have inverses (pratipaksha) but no identity element.
; group-like: inverses exist, but weaker than monoid (no fold guarantee).

(kosha op-class-binary
  (swarupa yantra dvi-ahara shuddhi)
  (sthita asama group)
  (yukta pratipaksha))
